   "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.header": "From specimen to engineered genetics",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_1": "Binnie's Genetics laboratory is a chain of specialised machines. The main route extracts a gene, identifies it, charges it into a serum, then applies it to another organism.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_2": "The Sequencer decodes the isolated sample. Fluorescent Dye is consumed as the readout advances, and a completed gene is added to the owner's genetic knowledge.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_3": "The Polymeriser adds charges to a serum using Polymerising Bacteria and Raw DNA. More genes cost more fluid; a Gold Nugget can accelerate the process.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_4": "Use the Inoculator for controlled serum application with Vector Bacteria, or the faster and much more power-hungry Splicer for serum arrays.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_5": "The Analyser reveals genetics, the Gene Pool turns organisms into Raw DNA, and the Incubator and Acclimatiser handle reagent production and environmental tolerance. Each has its own focused Ponder scene.",
   "binniecore.ponder.isolator.header": "Sampling genes with the Isolator",
-  "binniecore.ponder.isolator.text_1": "The Isolator takes a genetic individual and samples one active or inactive allele into an Empty Sequencer.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.isolator.text_2": "The live interface exposes the organism, sequencer, enzyme charge and ethanol tank separately. The machine can consume the specimen during extraction, so keep valuable breeding stock backed up.",
   "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.header": "Decoding genes with the Sequencer",
-  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.text_1": "The Sequencer accepts unsequenced genetic material and progressively identifies the allele stored in it.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.text_2": "Fluorescent Dye provides the sequencing charge. The live readout fills with decoded bases while progress is retained on the sequence itself.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.text_3": "When sequencing completes, the discovered gene is recorded for the owner and the Empty Sequencer can be recovered for another sample.",
   "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.header": "Charging serums with the Polymeriser",
-  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.text_1": "The Polymeriser turns a serum or serum array into a reusable genetic tool by adding charges, up to sixteen charges.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.text_2": "Its two horizontal tanks are Polymerising Bacteria and Raw DNA. Fluid demand scales with the number of genes in the serum array.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.text_3": "A charged Gold Nugget is optional: supplying one accelerates polymerisation rather than changing the result.",
   "binniecore.ponder.inoculator.header": "Applying a serum with the Inoculator",
-  "binniecore.ponder.inoculator.text_1": "The Inoculator applies the genes stored in a charged serum or serum array to a compatible genetic individual.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.inoculator.text_2": "Vector Bacteria is the carrier fluid. Successful processing returns the modified organism and removes one charge from the serum.",
   "binniecore.ponder.splicer.header": "High-throughput gene application with the Splicer",
-  "binniecore.ponder.splicer.text_1": "The Splicer is the aggressive alternative to the Inoculator: it works with serum arrays and processes organisms much faster at a much higher power cost.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.splicer.text_2": "Unlike the Inoculator, its application path does not require a Vector Bacteria tank. Use it when throughput matters more than efficiency.",
   "binniecore.ponder.analyser.header": "Revealing genetics with the Analyser",
-  "binniecore.ponder.analyser.text_1": "The Analyser identifies hidden information on an unanalysed genetic individual or sequence and records the discovery for its owner.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.analyser.text_2": "DNA Dye is consumed as a charged laboratory reagent. Analysed results can then be understood by Binnie's database and genetics tools instead of remaining opaque.",
